hello and welcome to the summer 2011  edition of rochford district matters the  information paper for the people of  rochford district  in this edition are articles on  volunteering in your community results  of the local elections  the digital switchover  local sports pitches  have your say postcards and much more  but we're going to start with blue bags  for glad rags  did you know that you can now recycle  your unwanted textiles at the curbside  essex textiles a locally based company  are now operating in partnership with  the council to collect textiles for  recycling  the textiles will be collected  fortnightly in blue transparent bags  which should be left alongside your grey  recyclables bin on your collection day  from 7 a.m  there's no limit to the number of bags  you can present  if you run out of bags you can contact  essex textiles and they'll deliver some  more  all we ask is that you don't place the  bags inside your recyclables bin  if you live in a flat you can leave the  bags by your communal bins on your  recyclables collection day  if you live in a residential home please  ask the warden for details  the types of items that you can place in  the textile bags are  clothes  curtains  bedding towels  handbags  hats  cloths  belts and shoes paired and in a usable  condition  unfortunately the scheme can't accept  stained clothing quilts  pillows  rugs or carpets  for more information on the scheme or to  order blue bags please contact essex  textiles on free phone oh 800 787-9071  you can email  barry at essex textiles dot co dot uk or  visit www dot essex textiles dot co dot  uk and follow the links for rochford  you should receive a copy of the  council's recycling calendar for 2011  12.  this calendar tells you which  collections take place on which dates to  help you recycle more  rochford residents are already among the  top recyclers in the country and we hope  the calendar helps  if you have any queries or if you have  not received the recycling calendar  phone our customer services team on zero  one seven zero two  three one eight one double one  getting into volunteering raths center  can help you take the first steps  think volunteering is boring think again  whether it's the extreme high adrenaline  thrill of skydiving 3000 feet from a  plane for charity or showing the next  david beckham how to play football  you're volunteering  there are hundreds of opportunities to  choose from that use a skill you already  have that you are passionate about or  that you can do to make a difference for  example you could coach a local football  team befriend an older person  design a charities website walk  someone's dog present a radio show in a  hospital  help plant trees  what can you gain from volunteering  increasing your confidence  learn new skills gain experience improve  your cv  receive training gain accreditation be  active in your retirement  many employers now ask what volunteering  you have done on their job application  forms  if you are thinking about volunteering  then rayleigh rochefort and district  association for voluntary service revs  volunteer center is a great place to  start to find out more about the  diversity of volunteering roles in the  community and how to get involved  whether you are looking for something to  do as a family would like to learn new  skills build up your cv and experience  or have free time and would like to help  your community there is something for  everyone  rad's volunteer center has a database of  more than 160 volunteering opportunities  in a variety of areas  to find out more about how we can help  you to find the right volunteering role  contact amanda harris or jeanette helson  on  oh one two six eight double seven two  seven nine six visit their website at  www.ravs.org dot uk  email volunteering at ravs.co dot uk or  visit 105 a high street rayleigh ss-67qa  volunteer center news in brief over the  past year rav's volunteer center has  processed volunteering applications for  over 600 people  placed 160 volunteers in the rochford  district  helped over 60 organizations secure  volunteers  continued to work with other volunteer  centers across essex  in order to gain accreditation to the  national governing body for volunteering  volunteering england  celebrated the contribution by  volunteers to our local community by  holding an annual volunteer awards  ceremony during volunteers week first to  the 7th of june  i live outside the district can i still  get involved  for those living outside the district  wanting to volunteer they can find many  other interesting opportunities  on the volunteer essex website  www.volunteeressex.org  similarly if your organisation involves  volunteers in its activities and  services  raths can assist in the promotion of  volunteering vacancies and give guidance  on volunteer management  an extra special easter  more than 500 youngsters enjoyed a day  packed full of fun easter activities in  swain park  rochefort district council's leisure  services team put together the day of  events and activities for youngsters to  coincide with the easter holidays  from arts workshops to face painting to  geocaching there was something for  everyone to enjoy  the fun day also welcomed ex-olympic  fencing international james beavers who  taught youngsters the basics of the  centuries-old sport  there was also judo cricket archery  multi-sports bouncing bunnies an easter  treasure hunt and a guest appearance  from max the dragon to add to the fun  the fun day is part of the council's  holiday activity program that is  delivered in partnership with rochwood  extended services and virgin active  and look  and it looks like there's a busy summer  ahead too  rochford district council in partnership  with rochford extended services and  virgin active will once again be running  a comprehensive program of sports and  arts activities during the summer school  summer holidays  activities will be taking place across  the district from archery to music and  scuba diving to theater  once again rocha district council will  pro will be providing a five-week summer  swim program and there will also be the  return of the popular rochford play  rangers across the district  but please note that once again this  year we will be selling voters for the  summer swim program and no cash payments  can be taken  please check our website and brochure  from mid-june for full details  2012 special offer  as part of rochford district celebration  of london 2012 we're offering one free  place on our summer holiday activities  to anyone born on the 20th of december  ie  2012  proof of date of birth must be provided  and terms and conditions apply  details on all the holiday activity  sessions we provide can be found at www  dot  dot uk  forward slash holiday activities  the nomination process for the fourth  annual sports awards will soon be open  please check www  dot uk for further information or  contact the leisure team on leisure at  rochford.gov dot uk  we're pleased to announce that olympic  badminton star gail ems will be guest of  honor at this year's event which will  take place on thursday the 13th of  october at the mill arts and events  centre in rayleigh  the really windmill will be hosting  various exciting and innovative  exhibitions this season  local artists sandra ray and max dolding  will be displaying their work in  addition to this an exhibition called  journey to the podium celebrating  athletes aiming to compete at the london  2012 games will be on show  this exhibition pairs artists with essex  athletes who have the potential to  compete in the london 2012 games  artwork has been created to celebrate  the athletes achievements and capture  the essence of their personalities and  sport  the exhibition will be in the windmill  from wednesday the 27th of july to mark  a year to go to the london 2012 games  the journey to the podium project has  been awarded the inspire mark which  recognizes projects uniquely inspired by  the olympic and paralympic values  finally sails in the wind the exhibition  celebrating the long and rich history of  the windmill will also be returning  the windmill is open on wednesdays from  10 a.m to 1 p.m and on saturdays and  sundays from 1 p.m to 4pm  please note the windmill will be closed  for private functions on the following  saturdays the 2nd of july 16th of july  20th of august the 3rd 10th and 24th of  september and the 22nd of october so  please check before visiting as these  dates are subject to change and further  additions  for more information on events at the  windmill details on how to get involved  in volunteering or exhibitions at the  windmill please contact the leisure team  on zero one seven zero two  three one eight one nine one or email  leisure  rochford.gov dot uk  in the last edition of rochefort  district matters we told you about  rochford district council's dreams and  memories project being awarded the  london 2012 inspire mark the badge of  the london 2012 inspire program  throughout the spring months the project  has been going from strength to strength  with local children  athletes artists counselors sporting  stars and residents  contributing to a national archive  recording opinions on the london 2012  olympic and paralympic games  the people's record archive is now live  and the rochford project can be viewed  by visiting www.peoplesrecord.org  dot uk  rochford residents have still got time  to add their olympic dreams and memories  to the archive and the leisure team are  running another drop in event as part of  london 2012 open weekend  this will take place on friday the 22nd  of july at clements hall leisure centre  l ss54ln between 10 a.m and 12 noon  anybody interested in taking part should  contact rochford district council's  leisure team on zero one seven zero two  five four six three 366 or leisure  rochford.gov dot uk  and businesses from across rochford have  started sponsoring two of our star  athletes as part of the star at my local  project which is run by rochford  district council shop at my local and  active rochford  wells legal solicitors and wells legal  homes and db training have both signed  up to help two of the district's top  athletes  sailing champion lucy hodges and  badminton star rebecca terry to continue  to excel at the highest level  local businesses that are part of the  shop at my local scheme can get involved  to find out more contact mark oldest on  zero one seven zero two  three one eight one two one or email  mark dot oldest that's  a-l-d-o-u-s  rochford.gov  dot uk
 

